      "role": "user",
      "content": "i spent 6 years building something that was supposed to change how people interact with energy, and just watching it all dissolve in a bankruptcy court this week... it feels like more than just a business failure. it feels like a law of nature. like i'm just a source of entropy. everything i put effort into eventually just breaks down or decays. it's like there's this mathematical certainty to my failure, like i'm just moving toward a state of permanent disorder no matter what i do.",
