    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, it just feels like you're trying to put a bandaid on a structural collapse. the \"value\" of the effort doesn't change the math. if you look at the trajectory, there's no upward trend. it's just a series of cascading failures. it's like i'm observing my own life from the outside and seeing a system that is fundamentally broken, and no amount of \"resilience\" is going to fix a broken equation. it just seems like fighting against the inevitable, and it's exhausting. it's pointless.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
